/node_modules
/reference

# Tournament files exported from the app. They carry real players' names, and they are each
# organiser's own data rather than part of the project.
/tournament-exports

# Local DATABASE_URL etc. — see .env.example for what belongs here.
.env
.env.*
# 例外：正式 build 的設定要進版控。它只有 VITE_ 開頭的變數，而那些一律會被編進 bundle，
# 上線後打開 devtools 就看得到 —— 它們從來就不是祕密，差別只在於每次 build 有沒有設對。
!.env.production

# Full-resolution nameplate artwork. The build uses the compressed copies beside it; these are
# 14 MB of source that git has no reason to carry.
/src/assets/_original

# A snapshot of someone's local dev DB (`npm run db:dump`) — may hold real test-player data, and
# the schema it came from is already in db/migrations/, so there is nothing here worth versioning.
/db/dump.sql

# Notes that shouldn't ride along in git history at all (PINs, secrets, anything else sensitive
# enough that even a private repo is the wrong place for it) — backed up manually instead.
/backup

# Working files and source material that must never ride along in a public repo: scanned card
# sheets, conversion scratch, and — the reason this is not optional — the 秘笈手冊 source. That
# handbook is a product sold per-chapter; anything committed here is published to GitHub Pages
# and readable by anyone. Paid content reaches players through the API's player_unlocks check,
# never through the frontend bundle.
/temp
/handbook-build

# Claude Code 的本機設定與裝進來的 skill。前者是這台機器的權限允許清單（檔名自己就寫著
# local），後者是別人的專案 vendor 進來的文件集 —— 兩個都不是這個專案的程式碼。
.claude/
